From: KMediaVlc Android maintainers <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] android: render external ANativeWindow directly

The libVLC output callback already supplies the final application-owned
ANativeWindow. Advertising the NDK AImageReader and ASurfaceControl capabilities
for that external window makes MediaCodec render through an intermediate layer.
On HDR-capable Android devices that layer can replace the decoder buffer
dataspace with sRGB, turning HDR10 output into SDR.

Keep the AImageReader path available for VLC-managed Android windows, but disable
it for AWindowHandler_newFromANWs(). MediaCodec then falls back to the supplied
ANativeWindow and preserves its per-buffer BT.2020/PQ signal.

---
 modules/video_output/android/utils.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/video_output/android/utils.c b/modules/video_output/android/utils.c
index ef277c1..ace5400 100644
--- a/modules/video_output/android/utils.c
+++ b/modules/video_output/android/utils.c
@@ -768,6 +768,11 @@ AWindowHandler_newFromANWs(vlc_object_t *obj, ANativeWindow *video,
     awh->wnd = NULL;
 
     LoadNativeWindowAPI(awh);
+    /* Externally supplied ANativeWindows are already the final video target.
+     * Keep MediaCodec on that target instead of inserting an AImageReader and
+     * ASurfaceControl layer, which can discard per-buffer HDR dataspaces. */
+    awh->b_has_ndk_air_api = false;
+    awh->b_has_ndk_asc_api = false;
 
     awh->views[AWindow_Video].p_anw = video;
     ANativeWindow_acquire(video);
